chapter AFP

session RCU_Client = OpSem +
  description \<open>
    Client: the RCU inc() critical section, instantiated against the Episodic OpSem
    stack (W10 refactor).  Defines `prog_RCU` as Core-typed labelled `command` data
    over the REAL Core types (operand-generic; no per-PC `case`, no baked-in C /
    var_s / var_n, S7 dropped), re-exports the single generic per-command effect
    rule against the concrete program, and exhibits a steppable reachability chain
    over the loop-free init preamble.

    SCOPE: the loop-free OpSem fragment only.  The RCU retry / poll LOOPS are
    present in `prog_RCU` as rolled `While`, but stepping them needs the lb / loop
    rule (W8b, still open), so no end-to-end RCU safety theorem is claimed here.

    Imports OpSem session-qualified (which carries the two documented open spine
    sorries), so this builds under quick_and_dirty alongside the rest of the spine.

    The surviving generated mordor digests `RCU_prog_digest` / `RCU_inc_loop_digest`
    (provisional placeholder types, import only Main) are built by the legacy
    `MRD_C11_RCU` session (top-level ROOT), not here.
  \<close>
  options [timeout = 1200]
  sessions
    "Core"
    "MemSem"
    "EventStruct"
    "OpSem"
  theories
    RCU_Client
